   "source": {
    "label": "thm:main-res",
    "number": "Theorem (thm:main-res)",
    "quote": "Let $\\nu$ be a bandit with marginally $\\sigma$-subgaussian arms. Then Empirical Gap Elimination with parameters $R, \\bm\\lambda$ and $\\bm t$ satisfies $$ e^{\\text{EGE}}_T(\\nu) \\leq 2(K-1) \\lvert \\cS^\\star\\lvert R D  \\exp\\left( - \\frac{\\widetilde T^{R,\\bm t, \\bm\\lambda}(\\nu)}{144\\sigma^2} \\right).$$"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Error probability bound P(S_hat != S*). Recorded with probability 'high_probability' as it bounds a failure probability. Uniform allocation (R=1) is a special case mentioned in text."
  },
